course: dictionary
lesson: 9070
title: Slippery: more than wet floors
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Slippery has two meanings, and the words around it show which one is meant. The first meaning is smooth, wet or icy, so that it is hard to hold or to stand on without sliding. «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» Floors that are wet or smooth are hard to stand on, so this is the first meaning.
explain: The second meaning is about a person. A slippery person cannot be trusted and is hard to catch or pin down. Phrases use it too: «as slippery as an eel» means very hard to catch, and a «slippery slope» is one small step that leads to worse things.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Wet pool edges are slippery, so you should walk, not run.» Does "hard to stand on without sliding" fit? Yes, so the first meaning is right here. Always read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Slippery means smooth, wet or icy so that it is hard to hold or to stand on without sliding.
fact: A slippery person cannot be trusted and is hard to catch or pin down.
fact: «Caution: slippery floor» is a sign that warns you to walk carefully.
fact: Slippery surfaces have low friction, so things slide on them more easily.
fact: A «slippery slope» means one small step that leads to worse things.
exercise: «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» What does slippery mean here? | *Smooth or wet, so hard to stand on without sliding | Friendly and kind | Very loud | Sticky and warm
exercise: Ahmed says, «The man in the story is slippery, so he must be covered in slime.» What does slippery mean about a person? | Very tall | Always laughing | *Cannot be trusted and is hard to pin down | Covered in oil
exercise: What does a «slippery slope» mean? | A kind of playground slide | *One small step that leads to worse things | A safe, flat path | A steep hill covered in snow
test: «A bucket of water is a pond with steep slippery walls: a small animal that falls in cannot climb out.» What makes the walls slippery? | Made of soft wool | Covered in leaves | Warm and dry | *Smooth and wet, so the animal cannot grip
test: «Wet pool edges are slippery, so you should walk, not run.» What should you do near a pool? | Sit down and sleep | Dive in | Run as fast as you can | *Walk, do not run
exam: «As slippery as an eel» means what? | Very short | *Very hard to catch | Very warm | Very loud
